(404521, 34624, 11073, '<td valign="top">cool pic.  I might have liked to see the shadow going the other direction...but that''s just me. focus is good.</td>', 'cool pic.  I might have liked to see the shadow going the other direction...but that''s just me. focus is good.', '2003-08-30 06:45:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(404522, 35073, 11073, '<td valign="top">good dof, and composition.</td>', 'good dof, and composition.', '2003-08-30 06:46:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(404523, 34853, 11073, '<td valign="top">very cool shot...i take it the lens was removed?  I''d be interested to see what it would look like with it in...but I''m sure that''s why you chose to do without =`)</td>', 'very cool shot...i take it the lens was removed?  I''d be interested to see what it would look like with it in...but I''m sure that''s why you chose to do without =`)', '2003-08-30 06:48:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(404524, 34924, 11073, '<td valign="top">very cool shot.  nice perspective, angle of shot, composition and the cord adds more interest to the shot.  nice work.</td>', 'very cool shot.  nice perspective, angle of shot, composition and the cord adds more interest to the shot.  nice work.', '2003-08-30 06:49:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(404525, 35202, 11073, '<td valign="top">I think that placing this on a workbench or somewhere more rugged than a bed would have lent better to the background and the overall feel to the picture.  The subject is good, the composition is there ( minus the tool sinking into the bed) and the lighting is there.  did the latch on the left break off?...or did you think it was too red?  I''m not the best photographer by any stretch...but I think it''s just the background that mainly hurts this imo.  When I first started taking shots around the house, I would always agonize about the background cause I never had anything good...then surfing the web it came to me...a trip to wal mart...and a dollar for a white poster board...and walla...instant "studio" =`)  But that''s just my opinion...that and a dollar will get you....well not much :)</td>', 'I think that placing this on a workbench or somewhere more rugged than a bed would have lent better to the background and the overall feel to the picture.  The subject is good, the composition is there ( minus the tool sinking into the bed) and the lighting is there.  did the latch on the left break off?...or did you think it was too red?  I''m not the best photographer by any stretch...but I think it''s just the background that mainly hurts this imo.  When I first started taking shots around the house, I would always agonize about the background cause I never had anything good...then surfing the web it came to me...a trip to wal mart...and a dollar for a white poster board...and walla...instant "studio" =`)  But that''s just my opinion...that and a dollar will get you....well not much :)', '2003-08-30 07:02:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(404526, 35088, 11073, '<td valign="top">focus...did you resize possibly, or use digital zoom?  The lighting is good, the composition is there as well.</td>', 'focus...did you resize possibly, or use digital zoom?  The lighting is good, the composition is there as well.', '2003-08-30 07:03:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(404527, 34779, 11073, '<td valign="top">cool shot - nice lighting, composition, focus/clarity, and texture in the tools.  nice work.</td>', 'cool shot - nice lighting, composition, focus/clarity, and texture in the tools.  nice work.', '2003-08-30 07:05:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(404529, 34735, 11073, '<td valign="top">good shot...the background looks a little overexposed - like where it meets the handle on the right...but that''s just a minor comment.  nice work.</td>', 'good shot...the background looks a little overexposed - like where it meets the handle on the right...but that''s just a minor comment.  nice work.', '2003-08-30 07:06:26.000000', NULL, 1),
